WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.477 --> 00:00:16.185
Lottie couldn't understand why Sara didn't wear pretty dresses anymore.

2
00:00:17.585 --> 00:00:19.186
Or why Sara had to work now.

3
00:00:19.206 --> 00:00:23.489
"There's a new girl in your room," Lottie said to Sara.

4
00:00:23.509 --> 00:00:25.430
"Where do you sleep?"

5
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.111
"Don't worry.

6
00:00:27.131 --> 00:00:30.576
I have a room," said Sara.

7
00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.498
But she wouldn't tell Lottie where it was.

8
00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:35.720
Lottie was determined to find out.

9
00:00:37.661 --> 00:00:40.784
She listened to the older girls talking, and then she knew.

10
00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:44.967
Late one afternoon she climbed the stairs to the attic.

11
00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:48.009
She opened a door.

12
00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:52.712
There was Sara, standing on a table and looking out the skylight.

13
00:00:52.732 --> 00:00:57.896
"Sara!" Lottie looked horrified at the bare and empty attic.

14
00:00:59.064 --> 00:01:00.565
"This room is so ugly!"

15
00:01:00.585 --> 00:01:02.967
"Shh, Lottie!"

16
00:01:03.387 --> 00:01:04.288
Sara said quickly.

17
00:01:04.308 --> 00:01:08.251
"Don't cry or make any noise.

18
00:01:08.611 --> 00:01:09.892
You'll get us both in trouble.

19
00:01:10.473 --> 00:01:12.374
This isn't such a bad room."

20
00:01:13.755 --> 00:01:16.037
Lottie bit her lip as she looked around again.

21
00:01:16.057 --> 00:01:18.539
"Why not, Sara?"

22
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.024
Sara hugged Lottie and forced herself to smile even though it had been a hard day.

23
00:01:26.068 --> 00:01:30.292
Then she helped Lottie to climb on top of the table so they could look out the skylight.

24
00:01:30.312 --> 00:01:35.176
"You can see all sorts of things from here," said Sara.

25
00:01:35.196 --> 00:01:38.658
"Things that you can't see from downstairs.

26
00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:43.022
I wish someone lived in the house next door, but it's empty.

27
00:01:43.843 --> 00:01:47.245
If a person looked out the skylight in that house, we could talk."

28
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.929
Two sparrows twittered and hopped about on the roof.

29
00:01:51.949 --> 00:01:54.912
"I see birds!"

30
00:01:55.408 --> 00:01:56.288
exclaimed Lottie.

31
00:01:56.308 --> 00:01:59.850
"I wish we could feed them," said Sara.

32
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.010
"I have a bun from lunch!"

33
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.271
Lottie shrieked.

34
00:02:04.171 --> 00:02:05.731
She pulled a bun from her pocket.

35
00:02:06.772 --> 00:02:09.593
The two girls broke the bun into pieces and fed the birds.

36
00:02:09.613 --> 00:02:14.094
"Oh, I like it here!"

37
00:02:14.574 --> 00:02:15.194
said Lottie.

38
00:02:15.214 --> 00:02:17.695
"It's much nicer than downstairs."

39
00:02:18.976 --> 00:02:19.796
Sara nodded.

40
00:02:20.456 --> 00:02:26.299
"It's so little, and high above everything, it's like a nest in a tree," she said.

41
00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:31.001
"In the morning I can lie in bed and look right up at the sky.

42
00:02:31.521 --> 00:02:34.923
And if there are stars at night, I can lie here and count them."

43
00:02:34.943 --> 00:02:37.744
"I'd like to live here too!"

44
00:02:38.304 --> 00:02:39.085
Lottie declared.

45
00:02:41.306 --> 00:02:42.106
Sara laughed.

46
00:02:42.126 --> 00:02:44.227
"It's time for you to go, Lottie.

47
00:02:44.647 --> 00:02:46.328
I don't want anyone to find you here."

48
00:02:49.348 --> 00:02:52.131
Sara helped Lottie off the table and out the door.

49
00:02:55.113 --> 00:02:57.055
Then she sat and looked around the room.

50
00:02:58.436 --> 00:03:01.999
Without Lottie, it was much harder to pretend her room was nice.

51
00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.862
The bed was hard and covered with a dingy blanket.

52
00:03:06.783 --> 00:03:11.967
The floor was cold and bare, and the footstool with the injured leg was the only seat in

53
00:03:12.007 --> 00:03:12.407
the room.

54
00:03:12.428 --> 00:03:17.492
"Sometimes this is the loneliest place in the world," she said.

55
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.661
Just then she heard a little noise.

56
00:03:22.381 --> 00:03:25.822
A large rat stood quite close to her, sniffing the air.

57
00:03:27.042 --> 00:03:30.423
Another child might have jumped back, but Sara stayed still.

58
00:03:31.884 --> 00:03:34.485
The rat could smell some crumbs that Lottie had dropped.

59
00:03:37.085 --> 00:03:41.186
The rat looked odd and strange, like a gnome with gray whiskers.

60
00:03:41.206 --> 00:03:46.528
"I won't hurt you," Sara said quietly.

61
00:03:47.796 --> 00:03:50.317
"Prisoners in the Bastille made friends with rats.

62
00:03:51.198 --> 00:03:52.338
I could be your friend."

63
00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.741
The rat came closer and ate a small crumb.

64
00:03:58.841 --> 00:04:01.623
Then he snatched a bigger crumb and ran into his hole.

65
00:04:01.643 --> 00:04:06.585
"He probably took that home to his family!"

66
00:04:07.145 --> 00:04:09.026
Sara was delighted with her new friend.

67
00:04:10.327 --> 00:04:11.867
"I think I'll call him Mel."

68
00:04:14.312 --> 00:04:17.894
Over the next week Mel gradually grew to trust Sara.

69
00:04:21.076 --> 00:04:23.257
She gave him food and never frightened him.

70
00:04:24.718 --> 00:04:26.599
One night Ermengarde came to visit.

71
00:04:29.321 --> 00:04:32.042
She sat on Sara's bed while Sara sat on the footstool.

72
00:04:32.062 --> 00:04:35.284
"I have a new friend," said Sara.

73
00:04:35.304 --> 00:04:38.726
"But you must promise not to be frightened by him.

74
00:04:39.466 --> 00:04:40.067
He's a rat."

75
00:04:40.087 --> 00:04:42.208
"A rat!"

76
00:04:42.856 --> 00:04:45.618
Ermengarde cried and pulled her shawl tightly around her.

77
00:04:45.638 --> 00:04:49.041
"He's very nice," Sara went on.

78
00:04:49.061 --> 00:04:51.302
"I call him Mel.

79
00:04:51.883 --> 00:04:52.923
Watch this, Ermengarde."

80
00:04:55.385 --> 00:04:58.768
Sara gave a low whistle, and Mel came out of his hole.

81
00:05:00.529 --> 00:05:02.130
She dropped some crumbs on the floor.

82
00:05:03.331 --> 00:05:04.432
Mel gobbled them up.

83
00:05:04.452 --> 00:05:11.652
"He always saves a few for his wife and children," said Sara.

84
00:05:11.672 --> 00:05:13.873
"They live in a cozy nest in the wall."

85
00:05:15.674 --> 00:05:17.715
Ermengarde was delighted by this story.

86
00:05:17.735 --> 00:05:19.096
"Tell me more."

87
00:05:20.117 --> 00:05:23.859
But before Sara could say anything, someone knocked twice on the wall.

88
00:05:25.159 --> 00:05:25.720
"What's that?"

89
00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.121
Ermengarde's eyes were wide with fear.

90
00:05:28.141 --> 00:05:32.123
"Just the prisoner in the next cell," Sara said.

91
00:05:32.143 --> 00:05:35.685
"Becky!" Ermengarde exclaimed.

92
00:05:35.705 --> 00:05:39.047
"Two knocks mean 'Are you there?'"

93
00:05:39.587 --> 00:05:40.488
Sara explained.

94
00:05:42.176 --> 00:05:44.178
Then she rapped three times on the wall.

95
00:05:44.198 --> 00:05:47.821
"And three knocks mean 'Yes, all is well.'"

96
00:05:49.022 --> 00:05:50.463
Becky knocked four times.

97
00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:53.666
"That means 'Good night.

98
00:05:53.826 --> 00:05:55.587
Sleep well,'" said Sara.

99
00:05:56.828 --> 00:05:57.789
Ermengarde beamed.

100
00:05:57.809 --> 00:06:00.031
"It's just like a story!"

101
00:06:00.051 --> 00:06:06.096
"Yes. You can be an escaped prisoner in the story," Sara told her.

102
00:06:06.116 --> 00:06:10.259
"But now it's time to sneak to your bed downstairs."
